WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Every day, weather centres
collect millions of observations.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.890
About 15 weather radars cover the
UK, each scanning every 5 minutes.

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.050
Far out in the North Atlantic,
moored buoys report every hour.

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:21.470
And 35,786 kilometres above the Equator,
satellites watch a swirl of cloud spin

5
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.270
in from the Atlantic.

6
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.270
None of them can see the future.

7
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.910
So how can a forecaster say rain tomorrow,

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.410
but not next month?

9
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.030
In this mission, you'll track
where weather data come from,

10
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.970
on land, in the air and at sea.

11
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.170
Then you'll read a synoptic
chart and a satellite image,

12
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.770
like a forecaster.

13
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.650
Your mission: find out why a forecaster
can promise tomorrow's rain but not next

14
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.370
month's.
